# This app only ever renders inside a Tauri webview — never the open web — so
# the targets are those webviews and nothing else.
#
# Tauri does NOT bundle a browser, which is the whole reason the installer is
# small; it borrows the OS one. That means two engines, not one:
#   • Windows  — WebView2, evergreen Chromium, and the platform this ships to.
#   • macOS    — WKWebView, i.e. Safari, and the platform it is developed on.
# Safari is the binding constraint and the reason this file cannot just name a
# Chrome version: a feature that works all day in the dev DMG can still be
# missing on the shipped target, and vice versa.
#
# The floors are Angular 21's own supported baseline. They were once dictated by
# Material's `mat.theme()` emitting CSS `light-dark()`, which is unpolyfillable
# and needed Chromium 123; Ionic emits none, so that constraint retired with the
# Material dependency.
#
# Do NOT write `last N Chrome versions`: that resolves to today's Chrome, far
# ahead of what a given Windows install actually has, so the build would stop
# downlevelling for the runtime it targets.
chrome >= 111
safari >= 16.4
